WEBVTT

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.318
Eep.

00:00:13.368 --> 00:00:16.806
[pops lips]
So, who's ready for dessert?

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.678
I told you, we're not hungry!

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.159
You ate a banana?

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:25.336
Nuh-uh. We ate all the bananas.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:27.512
[laughs]

00:00:27.686 --> 00:00:29.558
Uh, that's impossible.

00:00:29.732 --> 00:00:31.560
Not for cave people.

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.605
What have you done?

00:00:33.779 --> 00:00:35.651
They're just bananas, Phil.

00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:38.523
"Just bananas"?
"Just bananas," she says!

00:00:38.697 --> 00:00:41.048
That was my one rule!

00:00:41.222 --> 00:00:42.701
Wait, we're not done.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.530
There was more I was
planning on saying to you!

00:00:45.704 --> 00:00:49.578
Mrs. Better-mom, I'll just take
my dessert at the window.

00:00:49.752 --> 00:00:51.014
You kidding me?

00:00:51.188 --> 00:00:52.886
I'd live with her family
for how long?

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.932
With the... with the...
with the dirt and the smell.

00:00:56.106 --> 00:00:57.760
-[distant sobbing]
-Eep?

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:00.110
Eep, is that... you?

00:01:00.284 --> 00:01:02.591
[Phil sobbing]

00:01:02.765 --> 00:01:04.549
I don't know.

00:01:06.073 --> 00:01:08.118
-Did you hit him?
-No.

00:01:08.292 --> 00:01:09.641
I thought about it.

00:01:09.815 --> 00:01:12.601
The bananas were key
to our survival.

00:01:12.775 --> 00:01:16.692
The bananas
were keeping us safe.

00:01:16.866 --> 00:01:18.085
[continues sobbing]

00:01:18.259 --> 00:01:19.956
Safe from what?

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.219
[leaves rustling]

00:01:24.265 --> 00:01:25.657
PHIL:
It's here...

00:01:25.831 --> 00:01:27.268
for the bananas.

00:01:27.442 --> 00:01:29.009
Wh-What is, Phil?

00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:31.925
It has come every night
for a hundred moons or more.

00:01:34.666 --> 00:01:36.277
I found bananas are

00:01:36.451 --> 00:01:38.061
the only thing
that keeps it at bay.

00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:40.237
[crunching]

00:01:41.543 --> 00:01:42.979
[whimpers, gasps]

00:01:43.153 --> 00:01:44.807
What's on the other side
of the wall, Phil?

00:01:44.981 --> 00:01:46.809
PHIL:
Night after night,

00:01:46.983 --> 00:01:48.767
it was never enough.

00:01:52.032 --> 00:01:53.120
[screams]

00:01:53.294 --> 00:01:56.819
It wants its bananas!

00:01:56.993 --> 00:02:00.301
-What's behind the wall, Phil?
-[Phil gasps]

00:02:00.475 --> 00:02:01.867
-What is it, Phil?
-[whimpers]

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.914
-What are the bananas for?
-What is it?

00:02:05.088 --> 00:02:07.743
I don't know.

00:02:10.572 --> 00:02:12.878
[screaming]

00:02:13.053 --> 00:02:14.793
[scream continues]

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:20.103
-[scream fades]
-Huh?

00:02:21.713 --> 00:02:23.498
It's just a little punch monkey.

00:02:23.672 --> 00:02:26.588
-I'm leaving.
-[laughs]

00:02:26.762 --> 00:02:28.546
You just kept giving it bananas?

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.635
[Grug laughing]

00:02:30.809 --> 00:02:34.204
Wait, wait. Let-let me
understand something. [laughs]

00:02:34.378 --> 00:02:37.120
You had no idea
you were working...

00:02:37.294 --> 00:02:38.339
[laughing]

00:02:38.513 --> 00:02:40.297
...for an itty-bitty monkey?

00:02:40.471 --> 00:02:43.779
Giving it bananas...
[laughs]

00:02:43.953 --> 00:02:46.042
for years!
[laughing hysterically]

00:02:47.087 --> 00:02:48.653
[snarls]

00:02:48.827 --> 00:02:50.612
-[grunting rhythmically]
-[thumping]

00:02:56.835 --> 00:02:58.402
[both gasp]

00:02:58.576 --> 00:02:59.751
That's not good.

00:02:59.925 --> 00:03:02.189
-[monkeys shrieking]
-[both scream]

00:03:02.363 --> 00:03:03.538
GRUG:
No, no, no, no! Get away!

00:03:03.712 --> 00:03:04.800
[grunts]

00:03:04.974 --> 00:03:06.584
[grunts] Phil!

00:03:06.758 --> 00:03:09.587
[gasps, screams]

00:03:09.761 --> 00:03:11.633
Come on, come on,
come on, come on, come on,

00:03:11.807 --> 00:03:13.069
come on, come on, come on,
come... [grunts]

00:03:13.243 --> 00:03:14.505
[screams]

00:03:14.679 --> 00:03:16.681
[monkeys chittering]

00:03:20.859 --> 00:03:24.428
Oh, Douglas, those flowers
did not agree with me.

00:03:24.602 --> 00:03:26.952
-What'd I miss?
-[whines]

00:03:28.432 --> 00:03:29.651
Hey, Mrs. Better-mom,

00:03:29.825 --> 00:03:31.218
wasn't there
a wall there before?

00:03:31.392 --> 00:03:32.523
[Hope gasps]

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.092
Phil?

00:03:36.266 --> 00:03:38.225
Dad? Guy?

00:03:38.399 --> 00:03:41.010
-Grug?
-[groans]

00:03:41.184 --> 00:03:43.491
HOPE:
It's gone. The wall is gone.

00:03:43.665 --> 00:03:45.058
Phil's gone.

00:03:45.232 --> 00:03:46.755
Oh, my gosh.
Something has taken him,

00:03:46.929 --> 00:03:48.409
taken all of them.

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:50.454
-What are we gonna do?
-THUNK: No sign of 'em.

00:03:50.628 --> 00:03:52.935
But I did find this, though.

00:03:53.109 --> 00:03:55.503
-Is that my basket?
-Good eye.

00:03:55.677 --> 00:03:57.809
Sandy can track them with this.

00:03:57.983 --> 00:03:59.463
-Sandy, seek.
-[Sandy growls]

00:03:59.637 --> 00:04:01.596
-[sniffing]
-HOPE: Okay, right.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.599
You guys go, and Dawn and I
will stay here and fix the wall.

00:04:04.773 --> 00:04:06.166
Or better yet, Dawn,

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.819
let's get you
back inside your panic cubby.

00:04:07.993 --> 00:04:10.692
In fact, I think we can
both fit if we suck it in.

00:04:10.866 --> 00:04:12.694
-[howls]
-She's got the scent.

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:14.826
UGGA: Whatever took them
couldn't have gotten far.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.132
[sighs]

00:04:16.306 --> 00:04:18.743
Mom, I'm going, too.

00:04:18.917 --> 00:04:20.484
Dawn! Listen to yourself.

00:04:20.658 --> 00:04:21.964
We are not like them.

00:04:22.138 --> 00:04:23.879
Dad needs us.

00:04:24.053 --> 00:04:26.229
Wait. Dawn!

00:04:27.361 --> 00:04:28.579
[sighs]

00:04:28.753 --> 00:04:30.842
Dawn, you'll need
the travel basket.

00:04:31.016 --> 00:04:32.801
It has a neck pillow.

00:04:32.975 --> 00:04:34.194
-[monkeys chittering]
-Where are you taking us?

00:04:34.368 --> 00:04:35.934
-[grunts]
-[grunts] Stop talking!

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.893
PHIL:
If you're going to eat us,

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:39.808
y-you should eat
the fat one first.

00:04:39.982 --> 00:04:41.331
He ate your bananas.

00:04:41.505 --> 00:04:43.116
GRUG:
Oh, don't you blame me for this.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.161
-This is all your fault!
-PHIL: My fault?

00:04:45.335 --> 00:04:46.597
Tell him, Guy.

00:04:46.771 --> 00:04:48.817
GUY:
She says I changed.

00:04:48.991 --> 00:04:50.601
[laughs]
I didn't change.

00:04:50.775 --> 00:04:52.560
This is the real me, baby.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:53.909
You know?
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:54.083 --> 00:04:55.563
-[screeches] -What you see,
that's what you get.

00:04:55.737 --> 00:04:57.130
That's what you...
That's what you...

00:04:57.304 --> 00:04:58.740
There you are.
I lost you for a second.

00:04:58.914 --> 00:05:00.133
Anyway, I don't need anybody.

00:05:00.307 --> 00:05:01.786
-[screeches]
-No one at all. Ow!

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.094
Fine. Wasn't much of
a conversation anyway.

00:05:05.268 --> 00:05:06.139
Guess it's just me,

00:05:06.313 --> 00:05:08.402
with my thoughts.

00:05:08.576 --> 00:05:09.751
Travel log.

00:05:09.925 --> 00:05:12.275
Literally,
I'm traveling in a log.

00:05:12.449 --> 00:05:14.364
So, it's been a while.
Little update.

00:05:14.538 --> 00:05:16.279
Remember that Tomorrow?

00:05:16.453 --> 00:05:18.760
You know, the one I spent
my whole life looking for?

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.414
[chuckles]:
Well, turns out

00:05:20.588 --> 00:05:22.372
the girl I love
wants nothing to do with it.

00:05:22.546 --> 00:05:24.069
-[Eep scoffs]
-Or me.

00:05:24.244 --> 00:05:26.376
Girls: very, very complicated.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.073
EEP:
Dear diary,

00:05:28.248 --> 00:05:29.423
Hey. It's me.

00:05:29.597 --> 00:05:31.251
Remember what I said
about fate?

00:05:31.425 --> 00:05:34.079
-Well, fate's dumb and a liar.
-GUY: Hmm.

00:05:34.254 --> 00:05:36.604
Fate thinks
it's better than you.

00:05:36.778 --> 00:05:38.736
Fate wants to stay with...

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.912
GUY: The Bettermans.
They're amazing.

00:05:41.086 --> 00:05:42.566
I mean, have you seen
their tree house?

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.090
EEP: What's so great
about living in a tree?

00:05:45.265 --> 00:05:47.484
GUY: Showers, instant fire,
so much food and...

00:05:47.658 --> 00:05:49.312
EEP [mockingly]:
"Privacy."

00:05:49.486 --> 00:05:50.531
Well, one thing's clear.

00:05:50.705 --> 00:05:51.967
-It's over.
-Over.

00:05:52.141 --> 00:05:53.229
-Fine!
-Fine!

00:05:53.403 --> 00:05:54.491
-Who cares?
-Not me.

00:05:54.665 --> 00:05:56.667
[both scoffing repeatedly]

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.324
Huh. Hmm.

00:06:01.498 --> 00:06:03.979
Are you okay?

00:06:04.153 --> 00:06:05.328
-Huh?
-[Thunk groans]

00:06:05.502 --> 00:06:07.112
It's so bright out here.

00:06:07.287 --> 00:06:08.723
I just need to watch
the window for a s...

00:06:08.897 --> 00:06:10.246
I just... I just need
to watch it for a minute!

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:11.813
-[whimpers]
-[growls]

00:06:12.857 --> 00:06:14.032
Oh. [grunts]

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:16.165
Hey, my travel basket.

00:06:16.339 --> 00:06:18.994
[sighs]
Travel window.

00:06:19.168 --> 00:06:20.517
Ugga, can you tell your son

00:06:20.691 --> 00:06:22.432
to keep his grubby hands
off my stuff, please?

00:06:22.606 --> 00:06:25.783
Listen, I-I feel really bad
about what happened at dinner

00:06:25.957 --> 00:06:28.351
with my parents and you and Guy.

00:06:28.525 --> 00:06:31.049
Oh. [scoffs]
Please, I'm good.

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:33.356
It's in the past!

